   "t": 1791261169.930608,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "The stop fired immediately after init with a single feature. However, a single-feature specification with Sharpe 1.4409 in-sample is a strong candidate, but I should be cautious: single-feature high in-sample Sharpe is more prone to overfitting noise, and I haven't explored whether a 2-3 feature combination is more robust (less concentrated risk, more stable). But my trigger already fired, meaning per my own declared rule, I should stop here.\n\nLet me think about this carefully. The rule fired as intended \u2014 this is a legitimate stop, not a restart situation. The single feature found by `init` achieved Sharpe 1.4409, comfortably above my 1.2 bar. This is a valid outcome of my search.\n\nGiven the stop fired, I will submit with this specification. Let me set a reasonable prediction for out-of-sample Sharpe \u2014 in-sample Sharpe from a single-feature pick without multiple-testing adjustment typically shrinks substantially out of sample, especially chosen as the max of 80 candidates (selection bias)."
